2d557","e60d0fe882f55d06","e6131a1723e17184","e63895b3045375e5","e63c9de14a3da637","e7a46387a0f381cf","e8f177854bde4311","e968202ff2657805","e9960278eb7434a1","e9d317e870ce4edc","ea1ef01803ac9575","ea393ba22fa6c2dd","ead87747e6e45ace","eb8dc1e8401bc1e8","eccbc49325f2e385","ed989ce5437c1164","edf9f07143caabf6","ef8340aa624d1e92","ef88bb7c409c618d","ef90165b2d471b05","ef90165b2d471b05","ef90165b2d471b05","ef90165b2d471b05","f0ea99a15175fb42","f15b660f49309233","f37f834e25a037ec","f3cd1109f8e3d6b9","f46d3a08ca9fb99c","f4dbf639ed3f31fd","f68c552a47d8edb3","f81c0d944fb041d6","f8621ad650c15587","f89959cfdc1df6ac","f8f28cdd91b1507f","f91b629caf755714","f9684201b515bee5","f9684201b515bee5","fa4cb473fcd76625","faa409b4c053a08f","fc3818194f849329","fde7b52945f59dda","fed6a14b3330b6af","ff325a082a7e00a6","ff7ee56faf3f15d8","ff7ee56faf3f15d8","ff7ee56faf3f15d8","ff7ee56faf3f15d8"],"groups":["9541e73c5384c793","af39d66c6d52c9a2","6fc2bf5aaae913af","9a8aa8a035d27e91","db77f76c653e3f05","41b1d2498c2312d4","3ce2611eb5947b9e"],"findings":"**Review of the batch-decision change (`--decide-template` / `--decide-file`)**\n\nI only read the code and grepped the repo. I did not apply any change or run the tests, so every point below is **read**.\n\n1. **Duplicated report lookup and unknown-ref warning** (`reviews.ts`, the `decide-template` block around lines 80–85, the `decide-file` block around lines 96–108, and the single-call warning at line 138).\n   - The template and batch paths each do `holdersOf(id).flatMap(readReviews).find(r => r.id === id)`. The batch path also repeats the \"no finding X\" warning that the single-call path already prints at line 138, in nearly the same words.\n   - Suggestion: extract `reportOf(id)` and `warnUnknownRef(id, ref, where)`, and use them in all three places.\n   - Benefit: one message to keep consistent, and one lookup to get right.\n   - Size: small, about 15 lines moved.\n\n2. **Two parallel structures in `scan` for the refs and their texts** (`findings.ts` h9–h13).\n   - `scan` now returns `refs` and a parallel `texts` array. `findingTexts` then dedupes them with a `seen` set and a `flatMap` trick, while `findingRefs` builds a Set from `refs` separately.\n   - Suggestion: have `scan` record a `Map<ref, text>` with first-wins (`if (!m.has(ref)) m.set(ref, text)`). Then `findingTexts` returns `[...m]`, and `findingRefs` returns `new Set(m.keys())`.\n   - Benefit: no parallel arrays and no dedupe logic. The same ref can't drift out of step with its text, which the parallel arrays allow.\n   - Size: small, about 10 lines in `findings.ts`.\n\n3. **Dead `EOF` branch and a spin on `EAGAIN` in `readBounded`** (`batch.ts:31–34`).\n   - `readSync` reports end of input as a zero-byte read on Linux and macOS. The `code === 'EOF'` branch only matters on Windows, and the repo has no other Windows-specific handling. The `EAGAIN` → `continue` branch busy-loops on a non-blocking stdin.\n   - Suggestion: delete the `EOF` branch, and let other errors throw. If non-blocking stdin matters, handle it explicitly rather than spinning. Otherwise the loop is simpler as `readSync` until `n === 0`.\n   - Benefit: fewer branches to reason about. The spin is a real CPU cost if stdin is ever non-blocking.\n   - Size: small.\n\n4. **Entry checks partly repeat `checkDecision`** (`batch.ts`, `parseBatch`, around lines 72–82).\n   - `parseBatch` checks the finding, the outcome and the note by hand. It then calls `checkDecision` and rewrites its message. `checkDecision` already covers the empty finding, the outcome set, the length limits and `isValidDecision`.\n   - The hand checks are needed only to give the \"empty outcome\" and \"not a string\" messages a better wording. Those messages could instead come from `checkDecision` with the same wrapper.\n   - Benefit: one place to change the rules. I'd judge this lower-value than the others, because the entry-specific wording is useful to the arbiter.\n   - Size: small to medium.\n\nI did not look for a shared bounded-file reader elsewhere in the repo. The other `readFileSync(0)` callers (`reviews.ts` `--record`, `add.ts`, `carry.ts`, `sync.ts`) are unbounded and don't match this helper's needs, so there is nothing to reuse there.\n\nThe change is not lean, but it is not bloated either. Suggestions 1 and 2 give the clearest gain for the effort.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
